      <h2 id="article-heading">How Do You Calculate Your Exact Age in Years, Months, and Days?</h2>
      <p>Calculating your exact age requires subtracting your date of birth from a target calculation date. Because calendar months vary in length between 28 and 31 days and leap years add February 29th every 4 years, simple subtraction must account for month boundaries and leap year days.</p>

      <p>If you want to track remaining days until a specific upcoming holiday or anniversary, check out our <a href="/tools/days-until-date-calculator/">Days Until Date Calculator</a>, or use our <a href="/tools/date-difference-calculator/">Date Difference Calculator</a> to measure working business days between two dates.</p>

      <h3>How Are Leap Year Birthdays (February 29th) Calculated?</h3>
      <p>People born on a leap day (February 29th) face a unique calendar situation during non-leap years. Legally and mathematically, age turns on February 28th or March 1st during non-leap years. Our algorithm evaluates February 29th birthdays on February 28th during non-leap years to maintain consistent day counts.</p>

      <h3>Why Exact Age Verification Matters</h3>
      <p>Knowing your precise age in days and months is required for numerous legal and administrative purposes:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Passport &amp; Driver's License Issuance:</strong> Identifying exact qualification thresholds for minor versus adult identification cards.</li>
        <li><strong>School Enrollment &amp; Sports Leagues:</strong> Determining academic grade eligibility based on cutoff birth dates (e.g. September 1st cutoffs).</li>
        <li><strong>Retirement &amp; Social Security Planning:</strong> Tracking precise eligibility months (e.g. 66 years and 6 months full retirement age).</li>
      </ul>

      <p>When computing financial budgets for milestone birthday celebrations, you can calculate discounts with our <a href="/tools/discount-calculator/">Discount Calculator</a> or verify password security for online accounts with our <a href="/tools/password-generator/">Strong Password Generator</a>.</p>
    </article>

